(b) to propagate Buddha Dhamma by holding worshipservices and to transmit the Maitreyan Tri- ratna byperforming the relevant rituals ;

(c) to uplift and improve the socio- economic conditionsof the people of Sri Lanka and help them attain ahigher life by propagating Buddha Dharma ;

(d) to provide financial aid and award scholarships tochildren in indigant conditions and grant financialaid and assistance in any other form, for theadvancement, of education and knowledge,including the establishment of libraries and culturalcentres ;

(e) to collaborate or amalgamate with any otherinstitution or organization, whether foreign orlocal, having objects similar to those of theCorporation ;

(f) to conduct and sponsor conferences, lectures,seminars, workshops and group studies within oroutside Sri Lanka for the purpose of achieving theobjects of the Corporation ;

(g) to print, publish and distribute books, journals, bills,news papers and magazines which the Corporationmay consider desirable for the promotion andadvancement of its objects ;

(h) to establish vocational tranining centres andconduct training programmes with a view toproviding employment for youth ; and

(i) to generally do all such acts and things as arenecessary for, or incidental or conducive to thecarrying out or the attainment of the objects of theCorporation.

