(b) to builed up the capacity of such organisations;

(c) to promote the educations of the under privileged;

(d) to carry out relief, rehabilitation and reconstructionprogrammes;

(e) to promote health education, and to provideinformation on the eradication of malnutrition;

(f) to further, the welfare and development of theunder privileged;

(g) to promote income generating projects in theplantations as well as in the villages, and to launchself help projects, with a view to generatingemployment;

(h) to provide assistance to relive distress caused bynatural disasters such as floods, cyclones anddroughts ;

(i) to disseminate knowledge and information onimproved methods of agriculture , horticultureaquaculture, sericulture, animal husbandry, freshwater fisheries and bee keeping, through thepublication and distribution of books andpamphlets and the conduct of seminars, workshops,lectures and film shows;

(j) to promote thrift among the under privileged.

